  "limitations": [
    "v0.13.1 binds published native beta.2 source 7a25cd72, both fresh qualified packages/profiles, the unchanged RTX 5090 beta.2 runtime/profile and stock OMP 18.12.6. Runtime/installability eligibility grants no native/product-tooling council approval, candidate-bound public-route acceptance or product publication. Root authority stays on published v0.13.0 until the lead lane pin.",
    "The client is unmodified upstream OMP and has no appliance commands; supported installation/lifecycle routes measure model/image identities before launch. Manually bypassed identity-asserting launches are not certified.",
    "All lanes bind published model version 3, 81f924d4. Native schema 3 stores use session-checkpoints-v3 under each immutable release instance's own cache root; never scan/import/migrate prior native generations. Keep old model/root bytes untouched and replay authoritative OMP transcripts. The unchanged RTX 5090 retains its compatible /checkpoints-v013 store; its v0.12.x roots remain isolated.",
    "Strict origin authentication requires a checkpoint root and API key at least 32 bytes. MACs prove origin/content, not monotonic freshness: a filesystem writer can replay an older authentic generation. No anti-replay authority is claimed.",
    "Checkpointing is best effort. A crash or expired graceful wait can lose unpublished acceleration state. Finite native import/hash work can delay decode; removing the Responses-lock cycle and accounting for off-worker export leases does not remove every worker I/O or latency cost.",
    "Within one API-key principal, prompt_cache_key names a session capability; use unique high-entropy keys and do not share that principal among mutually untrusted clients.",
    "Fresh native beta.2 normal/pressure product protocol and source-bound lane receipts support Chat/Responses JSON-schema output, 128-character tool names, status schema 2 and request-log schema 30. New public-route acceptance and native/product-tooling council remain separate; no predecessor receipt or carried RTX 5090 approval transfers.",
    "The strict RTX 5090 profile has 146368 automatic BF16 KV tokens, 131072 context, DFlash2 K=7, two active lanes plus two extra device-state slots, and 180-second pending timeout. Two requests run together only while prompts/output reservations fit; no constant-batch-two, universal warm reuse or prefill/decode fairness guarantee.",
    "Native shapes remain 131072 context/KV, INT8 MTP3 C1, strict origin authentication and UUID-bound sequential serving on port 18082. RTX 4090 uses 640 MiB admission headroom, two extra device-state slots and 15506063360 Host bytes; RTX 3090 uses 768 MiB, four extra slots, 12284837888 Host bytes and a 300 W serving policy. No native DFlash2, vision or smaller-host qualification is claimed.",
    "Windows K6 acknowledges NTFS ntfs-write-through, not POSIX fsync or arbitrary-filesystem/power-loss equivalence. Failed publication may retain an unreferenced or possibly visible generation. Capacity preserves the first I/O cause and surviving Responses objects; bounded rearm still requires Engine/admission progress, not external disk reclamation alone. Explicit client retry after reclaim remains possible.",
    "The unchanged RTX 5090 retains v0.13.0's deferred durable-owner/session-gate metadata churn, bounded stale-publication orphan work and workflow base-receipt cross-checking gaps. The native Windows port does not claim to close those unchanged-subject residuals.",
    "Powered quality/leak/global output parity, historical OMP parallel/fanout/warm-arrival latency, and full G2 after canonical serialization/F2 are not re-measured for this composition. EXP-097 retains its actual c2dbcbae/model subject and 5090-only policy; no native speedup/parity inference is made.",
    "Multi-GPU inference, simultaneous supported native serving, multi-tenant operation, priority guarantees and silent cloud fallback are unsupported. Brief isolated paired-controller tests are not concurrent public-serving qualification. macOS remains preview; Linux client evidence is WSL2-scoped. Native rollback uses only actual qualified lineage; the old RTX 3090 two-direction result is not inherited by the rebase."
  ],
